# Shared Pattern links (https://miiitime.com/p/{uuid}) are the same single-page
# app as "/": serve index.html and let the app read the id from the URL.
# Deliberately scoped to /p/* only -- not a catch-all -- so it can't shadow
# /.well-known/apple-app-site-association or any real asset.
/p/*  /index.html  200

# Party Join links (https://miiitime.com/join/{code}) -- same reasoning as
# /p/* above. Previously these were built on miiitime.app, a domain with no
# DNS at all, so no Party link could ever have opened a working page; this is
# what makes the miiitime.com version actually resolve.
/join/*  /index.html  200

# The app itself: https://miiitime.com/ is the public marketing site,
# https://miiitime.com/app is the actual Miiitime application (see
# BOOT_IS_APP_PATH / isAppRoute in App()). Same "serve the one index.html and
# let the app read its own URL" shape as /p/* and /join/* above -- there's no
# app/index.html file to fall back to. Bare /app plus /app/* (not just the
# bare path) so a stray trailing slash or future deep link under it still
# resolves instead of 404ing.
/app  /index.html  200
/app/*  /index.html  200
